DECODE_THROUGHPUT_STAGE name=inter_mc_dpb_deblock_product_writeback status=unknown cycles_per_mb=UNKNOWN note=Inter correctness, DPB fetch, deblock, and product DDR writeback are not fully represented by this ratchet yet.
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_STAGE name=parse_cavlc status=measured cycles_per_mb=3.230 method=stub_busy rise to fs_wr_reset transition per VCL frame note=Annex-B parse, SPS/PPS/slice header, CAVLC residual decode latency. Overlaps with ioctl byte injection in the testbench.
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_STAGE name=dequant_idct status=measured cycles_per_mb=0.000 method=combinational — h264_dequant4x4 + h264_idct4x4 + h264_recon4x4 are pure comb logic note=Zero clock cycles. Dequant/IDCT/recon are combinational modules instantiated in decode_stub; they settle within one clock period and consume no pipeline stages.
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_STAGE name=intra_pred status=measured cycles_per_mb=0.000 method=combinational — DC Intra_4x4 prediction is pred=128 constant note=Zero additional clock cycles. Intra prediction is currently DC-only (pred=128), computed combinationally inside h264_recon4x4. The parse_cavlc time already covers the residual decode; intra adds no pipeline latency.
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_STAGE name=diagnostic_paint status=measured cycles_per_mb=256.000 method=fs_wr_reset to fs_swap transition per VCL frame note=NOT PRODUCTION. decode_stub paints WxH=624x480 diagnostic pixels per frame at 1 pixel/cycle. This will not exist in the production decoder.
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_STAGE name=mc_interpolation status=not_implemented cycles_per_mb=UNKNOWN note=NOT IMPLEMENTED. Budget allocation: 250 cycles/MB (no adjacent-MB overlap). Includes DDR reference fetch (~100 beats with arbitration) and qpel 6-tap interpolation compute. This is the single largest stage and the primary schedule risk.
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_STAGE name=deblock status=not_implemented cycles_per_mb=UNKNOWN note=NOT IMPLEMENTED. Budget allocation: 100 cycles/MB for 16 luma edges + chroma at ~6 cycles/edge with BS/threshold/filter pipeline.
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_STAGE name=ddr_write status=not_implemented cycles_per_mb=UNKNOWN note=NOT IMPLEMENTED. Budget allocation: 50 cycles/MB for 48 coalesced 64-bit beats plus arbitration overhead.
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_STAGE name=injection_overhead status=measured cycles_per_mb=10.021 method=ioctl feedByte loop: 2 cycles per byte (ioctl_wr=1 then ioctl_wr=0) note=TESTBENCH ARTIFACT. Real hardware uses DDR DMA, not ioctl byte-by-byte injection. This cost does not exist in the product pipeline.
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_PRODUCTION_COST measured_production_cycles_per_mb=262.621 budget_cycles_per_mb=683.761 production_margin=2.6x
DECODE_THROUGHPUT_WARNING mc_interpolation/deblock/ddr_write are NOT IMPLEMENTED and NOT MEASURED. The margin ratio is computed against the aggregate cycle count which is dominated by diagnostic paint overhead (not production). The real production margin CANNOT be determined until MC and deblock are in the pipeline. Do not use the aggregate margin as evidence of timing closure.
